  "projectUrl": "https://efcore-encryption.com/",
  "published": "2026-11-05T16:27:40.507Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 10.3.0\n\n\t\t\tWHAT CHANGED SINCE 10.2.0\n\t\t\t- Licensing validation is back. 10.2.0 had it switched off, so it granted every feature with no key. 10.3.0 enforces it again, with one change from 10.1.0 and earlier: on a local development machine nothing is checked or logged, and every feature works with no key (before, a developer machine got a startup warning and the paid features were switched off). See LICENSE BEHAVIOR below.\n\n\t\t\tCORRECTION: CHANGES IN 10.2.0 THAT ITS NOTES DID NOT LIST (the 10.2.0 notes repeated the 10.1.0 notes)\n\t\t\t- New WhereBlindIn method for IN-list lookups on a blind-indexed column.\n\t\t\t- Stricter query guard: with UseEncryptedQueryGuard, equality (==, !=) and IN-list lookups (list.Contains) on a randomized (AES-GCM) encrypted column now throw EncryptedQueryNotSupportedException, because they silently matched no rows. Null checks, and equality on a deterministic provider such as the legacy fixed-IV AesCryptoProvider, are still allowed.\n\t\t\t- EncryptedQueryNotSupportedException constructor gained an optional fourth parameter, hint. Code that only catches the exception is unaffected. Code that constructs it must be recompiled (binary-incompatible change, source-compatible).\n\t\t\t- Fixed: MigrationCryptoProvider could fail to read about 1 in 256 legacy AES-CBC values whose first bytes looked like a GCM envelope with an unregistered key ID. It now tries the legacy decryptor first, and still reports a genuinely missing key.\n\t\t\t- Dependencies updated (see DEPENDENCIES).\n\n\t\t\tBREAKING CHANGES\n\t\t\t- Since 10.2.0: licensing enforcement returns (see LICENSE BEHAVIOR). An app that calls AddDataEncryptionML without a valid key will now fail at startup in production-like environments, as it did before 10.2.0.\n\t\t\t- Since 10.1.0: LicenseEnforcer.Enforce returns a new value, Outcome.AllowedInDevelopment, for an unlicensed local development machine under Auto mode (it used to return AllowedWithWarning). Code that switched on that result needs a new case.\n\t\t\t- Since 10.1.0: the guard change and the exception constructor change above. The net10.0 package requires Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore 10.0.14 or later.\n\n\t\t\tNEW AND REMOVED APIS\n\t\t\t- 10.3.0 added: LicenseEnforcer.Outcome.AllowedInDevelopment, LicenseGate.IsDevelopmentMode, and an optional developmentMode parameter on the LicenseGate constructor. Removed: none.\n\t\t\t- Added in 10.2.0: WhereBlindIn; optional hint parameter on EncryptedQueryNotSupportedException. Removed: none.\n\t\t\t- Also present in the 10.1.0 and 10.2.0 line: HasSearchIndex, AsEncrypted (WhereContains, WhereStartsWith, WhereEndsWith, OrderBy, ThenBy), EncryptedSortOptions, SearchIndexBackfill, UseEncryptedQueryGuard, WithNormalization and NormalizeForQuery, EncryptionRotator with RotationOptions and checkpoint stores.\n\n\t\t\tDEPENDENCIES (unchanged in 10.3.0; changed in 10.2.0 compared with 10.1.0)\n\t\t\t- Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore and Microsoft.Extensions.* (net10.0): 10.0.11 to 10.0.14. The net8.0 and net9.0 builds use the newest 8.0.* and 9.0.* patch releases.\n\t\t\t- MailKit 4.17.0 to 4.18.2. Microsoft.ML and Microsoft.ML.TimeSeries 5.0.0 to 5.0.1.\n\t\t\t- Security: MailKit 4.18.2 brings in System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs 10.0.13, which fixes advisories GHSA-846f-f764-76mx (high severity) and GHSA-2fmv-rv2c-59x7 (moderate) that affected the Pkcs version used by earlier releases.\n\n\t\t\tSTORED DATA FORMAT\n\t\t\t- Unchanged. Values written by earlier versions, AES-GCM or legacy AES-CBC, read exactly as before. Nothing needs re-encrypting to upgrade.\n\t\t\t- HasSearchIndex adds an optional nullable column named after the property plus SearchIndex. It needs a database migration and a one-time SearchIndexBackfill for existing rows. WhereBlindIn uses the existing blind-index column and needs no schema change.\n\n\t\t\tLICENSE BEHAVIOR\n\t\t\t- The license is checked only when AddDataEncryptionML is called. UseEncryption, blind index, search, sorting and EncryptionRotator never check it.\n\t\t\t- Community needs no key: field encryption, key rotation, cloud KMS, blind indexing, search and auto-encryption. Enterprise needs a key: ML classifier, Crypto Sentinel, email and webhook alerts, custom alert channels, decryption audit trail, compliance reports.\n\t\t\t- Local development (default mode Auto): everything works with or without a key, every feature is available, and no license warning or error is shown.\n\t\t\t- Deployed (Auto): without a valid key it throws LicenseValidationException at startup in Kubernetes, managed cloud, a container (unless the environment is Development), or when the environment is Production or Staging.\n\t\t\t- To log a warning instead of failing, set Enforcement.Mode to WarnOnly in the options, or set the environment variable EFCRYPTOML_LICENSE_ENFORCEMENT to WarnOnly. Paid features then stay off until a key is added. Strict mode fails everywhere, including a developer machine.\n\t\t\t- Plans: Community (free, under $2,000 annual revenue), Enterprise Annual ($2,999/yr), Enterprise 3-Year ($5,999 prepaid), Enterprise 5-Year ($6,999 prepaid), all Enterprise plans with unlimited developers and projects. See https://efcore-encryption.com/#plans\n\n\t\t\tKNOWN LIMITS\n\t\t\t- Sorting an encrypted column runs in the application and needs a maxRows cap. If more rows match, it throws and never truncates.\n\t\t\t- Contains search needs a term of at least 3 characters. StartsWith and EndsWith accept shorter terms.\n\t\t\t- The search index reveals which rows share short fragments of text, not the text itself. Use a dedicated blind-index key.\n\t\t\t- Existing rows are not searchable until SearchIndexBackfill has run. On PostgreSQL a trigram GIN index on the search column is recommended; the published timings were measured without one.\n\t\t\t- EncryptionRotator needs a single-column primary key and a concurrency token (or AllowWithoutConcurrencyToken), and stops on a row that cannot be decrypted.\n\t\t\t- Unicode normalization of search terms is not performed. Not tested: concurrent load, tables over 300,000 rows, MariaDB, managed cloud databases. The real-database tests ran on .NET 10 against PostgreSQL 16, MySQL 8.4 and SQL Server 2022.\n\n\t\t\tRoadmap: https://github.com/efcore-encryption/EntityFrameworkCore.Crypto.DataEncryption/blob/main/ROADMAP.md",
